course: dictionary
lesson: 4318
title: A big fish of the reef
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grouper is a big, heavy sea fish with a wide mouth. You can learn a lot about a word from the words around it, so read the clues. The sea, the reef and the rocks tell you where groupers live.
explain: «Groupers shake their heads at moray eels to invite them to hunt together.» The word hunt tells you groupers are animals that catch food. Eels, reefs and fish all point to the sea, so a grouper must be a sea animal.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. A grouper is a big sea fish, so «Groupers shake their heads at moray eels» still makes sense.
fact: A grouper is a big, heavy sea fish with a wide mouth.
fact: Groupers live in warm seas, often near coral reefs and rocks.
fact: The giant grouper can grow longer than a person.
fact: Some groupers change from female to male as they grow older.
fact: Some kinds are endangered from overfishing, and in Australia some are called «groper».
exercise: Where does a grouper usually live? | *In warm seas, often near coral reefs and rocks | In the desert | In cold, dark rivers | On tall trees
exercise: «Groupers shake their heads at moray eels to invite them to hunt together.» What does invite mean here? | *Ask to join in | Feed on | Hide from | Chase away
exercise: In Australia, some kinds of grouper are called what? | grubber | grover | *groper | grouse
test: What kind of animal is a grouper? | A tiny insect | A green plant | *A big, heavy sea fish | A bird that flies over reefs
test: Why might some kinds of grouper be endangered? | Because they live on land | *Because too many are caught by overfishing | Because they are too small to see | Because they cannot swim
exam: Read: «Groupers shake their heads at moray eels to invite them to hunt together.» What can you tell about groupers from this? | They live on dry land | *They hunt with other animals | They never leave the sand | They can fly
